<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Risan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rhizon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Risan is a small town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-kotor">Bay of Kotor</a> in Montenegro and the oldest settlement on the bay. As Rhizon it was a royal seat of the Illyrian kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardiaei">Ardiaei</a>, where Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teuta">Teuta</a> took refuge from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in 228 BCE. It became a Roman town, known today for the mosaics of a Roman villa, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> belonged to the Serbian principality of Travunia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/risan.jpg" alt="Risan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Risan,_Bah%C3%ADa_de_Kotor,_Montenegro,_2014-04-19,_DD_05.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 3rd century BCE the Ardiaean dynasty under Agron united the coast from the Neretva to Epirus, with Scodra (Shkodër) and <b>Rhizon</b> (Risan) as royal seats.</blockquote><a href="/state/illyrian-kingdom">Illyrian Kingdom</a></li><li><blockquote>Ruled by hereditary župans from Trebinje, it had towns such as <b>Risan</b> and controlled routes from the coast into the interior.</blockquote><a href="/state/travunia">Travunia</a></li></ul></section>
